<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Te Reo Māori (Aotearoa New Zealand) overlay — issue #210.

    Statutory context:
      * Te Reo Māori is an official language of Aotearoa New Zealand under
        the Māori Language Act 1987 (Te Ture mō Te Reo Māori 1987) and the
        Māori Language Act 2016 (Te Ture mō Te Reo Māori 2016).
      * The Treaty of Waitangi (Te Tiriti o Waitangi 1840) underpins the
        Crown's obligation to actively protect Te Reo as a taonga — an
        obligation Bios shares as a piece of software shipping to Aotearoa.

    Honest scope statement (issue #210 explicitly requires honesty here):
      This PR ships only the language-selector UI strings — those are short,
      use widely accepted vocabulary documented in the Te Aka Māori
      Dictionary and Te Taura Whiri terminology lists, and use macrons
      (tohutō) correctly.

      The clinical pattern explanations (sepsis screening, AFib burden,
      qSOFA, HRV, mg/dL ↔ mmol/L conversions) are NOT translated in this
      PR. Translating those without a fluent reviewer who also has
      clinical-translation training would risk losing the literature
      anchor and producing register-inappropriate or just wrong text.
      Empty keys would shadow the English default; instead, those keys
      are intentionally absent here, so Android falls back to the English
      pattern_strings.xml until a future PR commissions a qualified
      translator with iwi consultation (Health Quality & Safety
      Commission style guide; Te Aka Manawa; Hauora Māori clinical
      translation panel).

    Macron policy: use tohutō (ā ē ī ō ū) per standard orthography. Avoid
    double-vowel spelling. Words like kūmara, whānau, mātauranga, hauora
    take macrons consistently.

    DO NOT add translated pattern_*_explanation / _suggested_action keys
    to this file without iwi-consulted review. Better empty than wrong.
-->
<resources>

    <!-- == Settings UI strings (language selector) == -->
    <string name="settings_language_title">Reo</string>
    <string name="settings_language_subtitle">Whakarerekētia te reo pūnaha mō ngā kupu o Bios. He pānga ki ngā kōrero whakatūpato me ngā tapanga atanga. Whakaaratahingia anō a Bios i muri i te panonitanga.</string>
    <string name="settings_language_system_default">Te taunoa o te pūnaha</string>
    <string name="settings_language_apply">Whakamahia</string>
</resources>
